ricepilot doctor: 3 problems. nothing was changed; the commands are for you to run.

PROBLEM 1 of 3: <HOME>/.config/btop
  is gone: nothing is where ricepilot's link was.
  rule: SAFETY.md, the ownership predicate

  the ledger recorded a link here to
    <HOME>/rice/new/btop
  for profile `new`.

  something other than ricepilot took it away: ricepilot never removes
  anything, and when it stops managing a path it says so and forgets it.

  generation 0000, the one `rescue.sh` restores, had nothing here, and
  the link is in the script's attic:
    <HOME>/.local/state/ricepilot/attic/rescue-0000
  `rollback` records that; `switch new` would undo the rescue.

  run:
    # the rollback stops managing it, and puts nothing back
    ricepilot rollback
    ricepilot rollback --commit

PROBLEM 2 of 3: <HOME>/.config/foot
  points somewhere other than where ricepilot linked it.
  rule: SAFETY.md, the ownership predicate (fact 3: its target must match the ledger)

  it points at
    <HOME>/rice/old/foot
  which is inside profile `old`'s tree

  the ledger recorded a link here to
    <HOME>/rice/new/foot
  for profile `new`.

  ricepilot did not re-point it, so it is someone else's link now,
  and every switch refuses it.

  that is where generation 0000 had it, the one `rescue.sh`
  restores: most likely the script put it there. to record it
  again, set it aside and roll back to that generation —
  not `switch new`, which would undo the rescue.

  run:
    # set it aside (nothing is lost); the rollback links it again
    mv -nT <HOME>/.config/foot <HOME>/.config/foot.set-aside
    ricepilot rollback
    ricepilot rollback --commit

PROBLEM 3 of 3: <HOME>/.config/hypr
  points somewhere other than where ricepilot linked it.
  rule: SAFETY.md, the ownership predicate (fact 3: its target must match the ledger)

  it points at
    <HOME>/rice/old/hypr
  which is inside profile `old`'s tree

  the ledger recorded a link here to
    <HOME>/rice/new/hypr
  for profile `new`.

  ricepilot did not re-point it, so it is someone else's link now,
  and every switch refuses it.

  that is where generation 0000 had it, the one `rescue.sh`
  restores: most likely the script put it there. to record it
  again, set it aside and roll back to that generation —
  not `switch new`, which would undo the rescue.

  run:
    # set it aside (nothing is lost); the rollback links it again
    mv -nT <HOME>/.config/hypr <HOME>/.config/hypr.set-aside
    ricepilot rollback
    ricepilot rollback --commit

